MEASURED (these are data verdicts, NOT check failures -- the same
distinction AGENTS.md draws for score_preregistered.log):
  recall denominator identical : 50/50 documents
  gold sequence identical      : 29/50 documents
  (recall, order) both identical: 65/100 comparisons

VERDICT: SPLIT, and it splits AGENTS.md's warning in half.
  * RECALL is granularity-INVARIANT. The recall denominator
    len(set(gold)) is identical on every document, because
    compute_word_metrics joins and re-tokenises the GT. The
    specific cost AGENTS.md names -- 'changes the recall
    denominator' -- is FALSE, measured.
  * WORD ORDER (and NED, which is also sequence-sensitive) are
    NOT invariant: reading order is re-derived from box geometry,
    and line boxes cluster differently from word boxes.
  CONSEQUENCE for T1 section 4's three-quantity family: the PRIMARY
  quantity is safe. The two co-primaries are computed on a
  different footing for a line-annotated corpus. Paired
  per-document differences stay internally valid -- both arms of a
  contrast score against the same GT -- so this is a
  CROSS-CORPUS COMPARABILITY issue, not a within-contrast one,
  and T1 section 5's per-corpus stratification is what must carry it.
==========================================================================
SCOPE: measured on FUNSD with RECONSTRUCTED lines, because official
       SROIE is not on this machine. It establishes that the pipeline's
       reading-order step is sensitive to box granularity; it does not
       measure official SROIE's actual line annotations. Re-run against
       the real corpus before quoting a number from it.
